ned to use the  unset procedure  um  training for non-surgical embryo  transfer it can be  minimal or if you have a lot of  experience with mice or  sometimes if you're uncomfortable with  the procedure itself it's helpful to  take a class in this so there are two  different things that we suggest first  of all if you are an expert at handling  animals and you're comfortable with  the procedure itself  i would suggest either  starting with euthanized animals  or  you can also  practice on  animals that have been anesthetized  and if you are going to try something  like that  make sure that the animal is indeed 2.5  days pseudo-pregnant  the opening of the cervix has to be  dilated in order for the insect device  to pass through and so if you try to do  this without  without having the animal dilated first  it won't work  um and so i would suggest definitely  practicing if you're new to this  procedure practicing a few times without  embryos  because ambrose are precious  and i'm getting the hang of working with  maybe  euthanized mice first  and then moving on to  animals that  i i don't think that the  anesthetized mice are really necessary  unless you're really uncomfortable with  it but  moving on to animals that are uh just  pseudo-pregnant in a live format and  you'll find that it's an extremely easy  procedure to perform  if  anybody is interested in being trained  personally in this method  we do perform  workshops uh every year uh  internationally and locally um and we  can also  uh  do workshops on site if anybody's  interested in that and so um  it's it's a very easy uh  it's a very easy procedure to learn  okay  do you offer free insect samples  oh um we do actually offer samples and i  believe that it we have a booth here on  in the um  bio conference live and uh you can  actually request a sample at the booth  or you can request a sample from the  paratex website  and that's all the questions we have for  now  oh all right  well thank you again everybod